1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
A completed FEAT report is not automatically a valid analysis.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:13,199
It is a structured record that lets you review preprocessing, registration, model design, and statistical output in an evidence-based order.

3
00:00:13,199 --> 00:00:20,238
This video shows how to read that record before interpreting bright clusters or reporting a result.

4
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:23,940
Review the report in dependency order.

5
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:30,119
Begin with Pre-stats and ask whether motion, masking, and preprocessing outputs are plausible.

6
00:00:30,119 --> 00:00:34,397
Continue to Registration and inspect alignment across the brain.

7
00:00:34,397 --> 00:00:39,625
Then examine the design matrix, explanatory variables, and contrasts under Stats.

8
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:44,853
Only after those checks should you interpret thresholded results under Post-stats.

9
00:00:44,853 --> 00:00:50,556
A failure early in this chain limits what later pages can support.

10
00:00:51,406 --> 00:00:55,148
Write one defensible statement for each major dependency.

11
00:00:55,148 --> 00:01:02,164
For motion, describe the plot and any abrupt displacement rather than saying it looks fine.

12
00:01:02,164 --> 00:01:08,712
For registration, name anatomical boundaries and multiple slices that support a pass or concern.

13
00:01:08,712 --> 00:01:15,728
For the design, match columns to timing files and contrast arrows to the planned hypothesis.

14
00:01:15,728 --> 00:01:19,470
Specific observations are auditable; vague reassurance is not.

15
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:25,154
When you reach the results, keep the output types separate.

16
00:01:25,154 --> 00:01:28,539
A cope is the estimated contrast effect.

17
00:01:28,539 --> 00:01:31,923
A varcope describes uncertainty in that estimate.

18
00:01:31,923 --> 00:01:36,274
A t-statistic or z-statistic standardizes evidence relative to uncertainty.

19
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:41,109
A thresholded map displays locations surviving the chosen inferential procedure.

20
00:01:41,109 --> 00:01:52,712
Do not describe a z-statistic map as an effect-size map, and do not let an attractive cluster override failed motion, registration, or design checks.

21
00:01:53,562 --> 00:02:00,929
Finish with an explicit quality-control decision: pass, concern, or fail, followed by the evidence that supports it.

22
00:02:00,929 --> 00:02:04,829
Record any limitation and explain how it affects interpretation.

23
00:02:04,829 --> 00:02:08,295
Preserve the report, design files, and notes together.

24
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:13,061
The purpose of review is not to prove that FEAT completed.

25
00:02:13,061 --> 00:02:19,994
It is to decide whether this run can support the scientific claim you intend to make.
